  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="5093-098d-a6e2-9246" name="Standard Bearer" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Imperial Guard units with a model within 12" of the Standard Bearer may re-roll any failed Morale checks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="16d3-73ab-2527-3e33" name="Medi-pack" hidden="false">
      <description>Medi-packs allow a unit with a medic to ignore the first failed saving throw it rolls in every turn. The medi-pack may not be used on any model which suffers instant death or that has been hit by a close combat weapon that allows no Amrour save. It may not be used if the medic is in base contact with an enemy model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fcaa-7305-6950-d142" name="Comm-Link" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Command HQ or Command Section has a comm-link, then one squad with a comm-link each turn can use the Officer’s Leadership value no matter where they are on the battlefield (normally they’d have to be within 12"). You can use the comm-link anytime, such as right before a Leadership test or even if the command unit is still in reserve.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bfa6-639a-4ff4-e20e" name="Master-crafted Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>The bearer may re-roll one failed to hit roll per turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0630-f0bd-6da5-e593" name="Trademark Item" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit led by a person who carries a trademark item may re-roll any failed Morale or Pinning checks it suffers. However, if the character is slain, the unit must pass a Morale test to avoid falling back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c061-bcf5-ed69-d507" name="Scanner" hidden="false">
      <description>If enemy infiltrators set up with 4D6" of a model with a surveyor then the model is allowed to take a 'free' shot at them. If the model is part of a unit, the whole unit may shoot. These shots are taken before the battle begins and may cause the infiltrators to fall back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="468c-bd45-5505-589a" name="Immobile" hidden="false">
      <description>Once deployed, the model may not be moved unless towed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f779-54b0-691f-402d" name="Amphibious" hidden="false">
      <description>Treat all water features as clear terrain when moving</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3113-8762-7d4c-7334" name="Anti-Air" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll to hit aircraft using the firers normal BS</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8573-0653-d612-e4de" name="Smoke Launchers" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game, after completing movement, a vehicle with smoke launchers may trigger them. The vehicle cannot fire and use its smoke launchers in the same turn. Any penetrating hits scored by the enemy in the next Shooting phase count as glancing hits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4877-41b8-d9e1-6da3" name="Searchlight" hidden="false">
      <description>During Night Fighting missions, one enemy unit spotted by the vehicle can be fired at by any other Imperial Guard units in range and with line of fire. However, the vehicle using the Searchlight will then be exposed and can be fired at by any enemy units that are in range and line of sight of it until the next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="11ff-f612-addd-577e" name="Leadership" hidden="false" />
    <rule id="7023-343a-0f96-bd4e" name="Rough Terrain Modification" hidden="false">
      <description>A vehicle that moves no more than 6" may re-rolled failed Difficult Terrain tests</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="647d-f731-5d52-f8e4" name="Camo Cloak" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Tanith squad adds +1 to any cover saves they are allowed. In addition, opponents roll 2D6x2 instead of 2D6x3 when attempting to spot Tanith troops in a Night Fight.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="36d3-c20f-b78f-7bf9" name="Tanith Knife" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit led by a person who carries a trademark item may re-roll any failed Morale or Pinning checks it suffers. However, if the character is slain, the unit must pass a Morale test to avoid falling back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ea86-cee4-a47b-c214" name="Absolute Direction" hidden="false">
      <description>All Tanith units may re-roll failed Reserve rolls. If a Tanith unit is affected by a result on the Alaitoc Ranger Disruption table from Codex: Craftworld Eldar, roll a dice, the result is ignored on the roll of a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bcc1-8c37-a9c9-b60b" name="Holy Relic" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per battle. On any turn the model with the relic does not move they may reveal it. All friendly models that are within 2D6" gain +1 Attacks for the rest of that turn. The relic may be revealed in the opposing player's turn assuming the model with the relic did not move in the previous turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1973-df4c-dfdf-8af6" name="Bionics" hidden="false">
      <description>When a model with bionics is killed, instead place it on its side. Roll a D6 at the start of the next turn: on a roll of 6 the model stands back up with 1 wound, but on any other roll it is removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f1bf-49f9-4094-c2f9" name="Carapace Armor" hidden="false">
      <description>4+ Armour Save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b3db-ab15-ba69-979f" name="Refractor Field" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain a 5+ invulnerable save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1c37-d83d-2234-7c18" name="Targeter" hidden="false">
      <description>Models equipped with a targeter are allowed to pre-measure the range to a target before they decide who to shoot at in the Shooting phase. This ability must be used after all Guess ranged weapons have been used this turn, otherwise those weapons cannot fire this turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="23bf-b1d4-efd9-39e9" name="Iron Discipline" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit using the Leadership ability of a Cadian Officer with the Iron Discipline ability for Morale or Pinning test ignores the -1 modifier for being under half strength and may regroup even if below half strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0a5e-9493-a5b1-e5d5" name="Sharpshooters" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Cadian infantry model with a BS of 3 may make a single re-roll of a shooting to hit roll of 1. This has no effect when firing plasma weapons or sniper rifles.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="0b0d-c34d-0b36-560d" name="Deathworld Veterans" hidden="false">
      <description>Deathworld Veterans count woods or jungles as clear terrain. They receive a 4+ cover save for being in woods or jungle terrain. If they do not move in the movement phase may see and shoot through 12" of woods or jungle terrain instead of the normal 6". And they may infiltrate into woods or jungle in missions where infiltration is allowed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="32a8-a559-293a-a999" name="Opps, Sorry Sir!" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll a D6 for each Commissar before setting them up. On a roll of 1 the commissar has suffered an accident and cannot be used.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1e9a-8f2f-238e-9e34" name="Ambush" hidden="false">
      <description>See rules for Ambush set-up in Codex: Catachan page 20</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9d60-b109-f37e-cfa6" name="Gung Ho" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit may re-roll failed Morale and Pinning tests and can try to regroup even if below half strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1496-27c3-2f58-885c" name="Deathworld Toxins" hidden="false">
      <description>Deathworld Snipers may re-roll a failed roll to wound when using their rifles.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2150-cbd0-329c-5f33" name="Camouflage" hidden="false">
      <description>Deathworld Snipers have a 3+ cover save in woods or jungle terrain.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f24f-9916-55fe-8bf6" name="Disappear" hidden="false">
      <description>Snipers never move. During your Movement phase, you may remove the sniper, representing the Sniper merging back into the shadows. Once removed, a Sniper may not return to the battlefield but doesn't count as having been killed for Victory point purposes. Snipers cannot claim table quarters or other objectives and don't have to be killed for an attacker to win Meat Grinder or Grand Assault.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e3ad-147a-43f5-a00a" name="Set-Up" hidden="false">
      <description>See rules for Booby Trap set-up in Codex: Catachan page 21</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ef50-ea59-9c80-ccd7" name="Ignore Cover Saves" hidden="false">
      <description>Ignore cover saves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1644-75b3-7a1b-6398" name="Pinning" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit that suffers one or more casualties from a booby trap must test for pinning.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="dc13-2a4b-c609-d6da" name="Plasma Charge" hidden="false">
      <description>The model that triggered the charge is hit automatically.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8879-cace-77eb-a230" name="Shredder Mine" hidden="false">
      <description>The mine is located D6" away from the model that triggered it, in the direction indicated by the arrow on the Scatter dice. The player who laid the mine may place the flamer template with the narrow end at the location of the mine and positioned in such a manner that the model who triggered the trap is at least partially under the template. Any models touched by the template are hit automatically.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3d45-8e04-2e94-1f6d" name="Spring Mine" hidden="false">
      <description>Place the large Ordnance Blast marker so that the central hole is over the model which triggered the trap. Then roll for scatter in the same way as you would for ordnance. Any models that are fully under the Ordnance Blast marker are hit automatically, and any that are partially under the Blast marker are hit on a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8e6a-cb86-d10e-8502" name="Trap" hidden="false">
      <description>Place the small Blast market so that the central hole is over the model that triggered the trap. Any models fully under the Blast marker are hit automatically and any partially under are hit on a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0f0f-2dd1-567e-7c66" name="Placement" hidden="false">
      <description>Each booby trap you take allows you to booby trap a 1' square area.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5129-ecf7-d3f2-2a76" name="Jungle Fighters" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll 3D6 and pick the highest to see how far the unit can move through jungle terrain. When pursuing and falling back through difficult terrain, they roll 3D6 and halve the result. They only become 'spooked' on a roll of a triple one and only set off booby traps on any roll of a triple.
They receive a 4+ cover save for being in woods or jungle.
They may infiltrate into woods or jungles in missions where infiltration is allowed.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="53c9-3f47-f245-64d0" name="Ork Hunters" hidden="false">
      <description>Ork Hunters alway shit Orks on a 3+ in close combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="32c7-9250-c6eb-edca" name="To Know The Enemy" hidden="false">
      <description>When a squad of Armageddon Ork Hunters charges into close combat check its size by rolling 2D6. If the score is equal or less than the number of Armageddon Ork Hunters in the squad, they charge in with a rousing warcry to rival that to the Orks they fight. All Ork Hunters in the squad double their Initiative for the rest of the assault phase.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="0aa2-ad12-6696-1869" name="City Fighters" hidden="false">
      <description>If this unit is in cover then its cover saving throw is increased by +1 point.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="152e-3207-7d66-4964" name="Tank Hunters" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit always passes any tests for tank shock and adds +1 to all Armour Penetration rolls.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="28fc-a0b2-82ae-14c6" name="Citizens" hidden="false">
      <description>You may reroll any reserve rolls for this unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8fd7-c2ff-1577-b5d0" name="Sewer Rats" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit can use the special rules for Subterranean Movement to deploy, even in scenarios where these rules are not normally used.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d99b-425a-ce2d-e136" name="Stealthy" hidden="false">
      <description>This unit may set up using the infiltrator rules. If infiltrators are not allowed in the scenario being played then the unit may make a free move immediately after both sides have deployed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="48e9-280b-8702-e4d7" name="Cunning" hidden="false">
      <description>This unit may set up one booby-trap of your choice each game using the rules in the Cityfight book.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a39a-0e41-19fe-c0e8" name="Cityfight Veterans" hidden="false">
      <description>Cityfight Veterans may always roll one extra dice for their difficult terrain tests in the city.
Cityfight Veterans who do not move during the movement phase reduce their target's cover save by -1 in addition to any other modifiers.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="d5f7-46ce-8768-3e81" name="Hardened Fighters" hidden="false">
      <description>The Death Korp may ignore negative modifiers for Morale checks and tests for regrouping.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c9cc-854b-30e2-0c2c" name="Death Before Dishonour" hidden="false">
      <description>Death Korp troops are Fearless in close combat, automatically passing any Morale checks they are required to make, and will carry on fighting until they have beaten their foes or until they are all dead. Additionally, the must Sweeping Advance after an enemy that falls back.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="52f1-333b-4047-dc5c" name="On Time, On Target" hidden="false" />
    <rule id="3a78-7801-651a-d159" name="Gung Ho" hidden="false" />
  <rule id="56bd-9279-b9df-5645" name="Scavengers" hidden="false">
      <description>Savlar Chem-Dogs may never make a sweeping advance after a combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c75e-7f7f-5409-bb7f" name="Nitro-Chem Inhaler" hidden="false">
      <description>Savlar Chem-Dogs ignore negative modifiers to their Morale checks, and will test on the unmodified Leadership of the unit or character that is leading it all times.
In addition, if they do fail a Morale check, they will become pinned instead of falling back. However, they fall back in close combat as normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b0df-bc87-7a32-f38d" name="Chem-Riders" hidden="false">
      <description>All Savlar Chem-Riders benefit from an Invulnerable 5+ save.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
